      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬A⇒B.$",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional statement $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬A⇒B≡¬(¬A)∨B\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬A)∨B≡A∨B.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $A∨B.$",
